extends ../layout
//- Modified from sahat/hackathon-starter: the email/password, email-link,
//- passkey and social buttons are replaced by BuildBase's hosted page, which
//- offers sign-in and sign-up with whatever methods the org enables.

block content
  .pb-2.mt-2.mb-4.border-bottom
    h3 Sign in
  .row
    .col-md-7.offset-md-3
      if !buildbaseConfigured
        .alert.alert-warning
          | Set <code>BUILDBASE_ORG_ID</code>, <code>BUILDBASE_CLIENT_ID</code> and <code>BUILDBASE_CLIENT_SECRET</code> in <code>.env</code> to enable sign-in. The README walks through each one.
      p
        | Sign in or create an account on the secure sign-in page. Email, magic link, social login, passkeys and two-factor authentication are all there, as your BuildBase organization enables them.
      form(method='POST', action='/login')
        input(type='hidden', name='_csrf', value=_csrf)
        button.btn.btn-primary(type='submit', disabled=!buildbaseConfigured)
          i.far.fa-user.fa-sm.me-2
          | Continue to sign in
      p.mt-3.text-muted.small
        | Linking GitHub, Google and other accounts, to use their APIs in the API examples, is on your account page once you are signed in.
